      {
        "id": "sql-analytics.p1",
        "title": "SQL - Query Logic, Grouping & Joins",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "title",
            "text": "SQL - Query Logic, Grouping & Joins",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 38,
              "minFontSize": 29,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.16
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.title"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "1. Logical Query Order",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.s1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You write SELECT first. The engine runs it almost last. Most SQL traps follow from this one fact.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b1"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "SELECT aliases are not visible to WHERE or GROUP BY.",
              "WHERE cannot see aggregates. HAVING can.",
              "ORDER BY runs last, so it can use SELECT aliases."
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "2. WHERE vs HAVING",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.s2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Same keyword family, different stage of the pipeline.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b3"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "text": "WHERE",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - filters rows before grouping."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "HAVING",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - filters groups after aggregation."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "QUALIFY",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - filters window results (Snowflake, BigQuery, DuckDB)."
                }
              ]
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b4"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "3. GROUP BY Grain",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.s3"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The grain is the column set in GROUP BY: one output row per distinct combination. Change the grain and every aggregate changes.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b5"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "Every non-aggregated SELECT column must appear in GROUP BY.",
              [
                {
                  "text": "COUNT(*)",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - counts rows."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "COUNT(col)",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - skips NULLs."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "COUNT(DISTINCT col)",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - dedupes first."
                }
              ]
            ],
            "gap": 23.47333333333332,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b6"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "4. JOIN Types",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.s4"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pick the join by which side you must keep, then check the key's uniqueness.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b7"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "A join on a non-unique key multiplies rows (fan-out).",
              "Aggregate first, then join - never the reverse.",
              "Anti-join: LEFT JOIN ... WHERE b.id IS NULL or NOT EXISTS."
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p1.b8"
          },
          {
