      {
        "id": "sql-analytics.p2",
        "title": "SQL - Window Functions & CTEs",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "title",
            "text": "SQL - Window Functions & CTEs",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 38,
              "minFontSize": 29,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.16
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.title"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "5. Window Function Anatomy",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.s1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A window function adds a column computed over related rows. It never removes rows - that is the whole difference from GROUP BY.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b1"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "text": "PARTITION BY",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - restarts the calculation per group."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "ORDER BY",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - defines row order inside the partition."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "frame",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - picks which rows feed the aggregate."
                }
              ]
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "6. Ranking Family",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.s2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "All four differ only in how they treat ties.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b3"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "Deduplicate with ROW_NUMBER() ... = 1, never with RANK().",
              "Add a tiebreaker column to make ROW_NUMBER deterministic."
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b4"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "7. LAG / LEAD",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.s3"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Reach into the previous or next row of the same partition - the standard way to compute deltas and gaps.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b5"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "text": "LAG(v, 1, 0)",
                  "marks": [
                    "key"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " - offset then default; default is NULL."
                }
              ],
              "The OVER's ORDER BY is independent of the query's ORDER BY."
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b6"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "role": "section",
            "text": "8. CTEs",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 27,
              "minFontSize": 23,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "lineHeight": 1.2
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.s4"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A CTE names a step. It is readability first, and the only clean way to filter on a window result.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b7"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "A CTE is not a guarantee of materialization - plans may inline it.",
              "Recursive: WITH RECURSIVE in Postgres, plain WITH in SQL Server."
            ],
            "gap": 24,
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 21,
              "lineHeight": 1.32,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 20
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b8"
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "language": "python",
            "code": "SUM(amount) OVER (\n  PARTITION BY cust_id\n  ORDER BY order_date\n  ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW\n) AS rolling_3",
            "title": "Example - OVER(...)",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 16,
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 14
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b9"
          },
          {
            "type": "box",
            "variant": "note",
            "title": "Important",
            "text": "Default frame with ORDER BY is RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING - a running total.\nRANGE groups peer rows with equal ORDER BY values; ROWS counts physical rows.",
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 18,
              "lineHeight": 1.25,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 16
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b10"
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "columns": [
              "Function",
              "Values 10, 10, 9",
              "Gaps?"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "ROW_NUMBER()",
                "1, 2, 3",
                "n/a"
              ],
              [
                "RANK()",
                "1, 1, 3",
                "yes"
              ],
              [
                "DENSE_RANK()",
                "1, 1, 2",
                "no"
              ],
              [
                "NTILE(2)",
                "1, 1, 2",
                "buckets"
              ]
            ],
            "widths": [
              0.4,
              0.37,
              0.23
            ],
            "style": {
              "fontSize": 17,
              "lineHeight": 1.25,
              "overflow": "shrink",
              "minFontSize": 16
            },
            "id": "sql-analytics.p2.b11"
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "language": "sql",
            "code": "SELECT d, v,\n  LAG(v) OVER (PARTITION BY id ORDER BY d) AS prev,\n  v - LAG(v) OVER (PARTITION BY id ORDER BY d) AS delta\nFROM readings;",
            "title": "Example - previous observed value",
